          Collagen is the most heavily marketed protein on the shelf and the least useful one for building muscle. It is an incomplete protein: it has no tryptophan at all and very little leucine, so it cannot do what whey does. What it may do, according to a mixed and partly industry-funded body of research, is modestly support skin hydration and joint comfort. If you want collagen for those reasons, the best collagen protein powder is a plain, hydrolyzed peptide with a stated dose and real third-party testing. If you want muscle, buy whey. This guide covers both honestly.
        </p>

